  "text": "Here's a simple and classic recipe for **Neapolitan Ice Cream**, which traditionally consists of three flavors: **vanilla**, **chocolate**, and **strawberry**. This recipe makes a small batch, perfect for a family or a few servings.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf68 **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe**\n\n#### \ud83c\udf61 **Ingredients** (Makes about 4\u20136 servings):\n\n**For Vanilla Base and Chocolate Swirl:**\n- 2 cups heavy cream\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 3/4 cup granulated sugar\n- 1 tbsp vanilla extract\n- 1/2 cup dark chocolate (70% cocoa or higher), melted and cooled\n- 1/2 cup chocolate chips (optional, for extra chocolate chunks)\n\n**For Strawberry Swirl:**\n- 1 cup fresh strawberries (or 1/2 cup frozen strawberries, thawed)\n- 1 tbsp granulated sugar (or to taste)\n- 1 tbsp cornstarch (to help it set)\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1/2 cup heavy cream (or milk for a lighter version)\n- 1/2 tsp vanilla extract\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\uddfd **Instructions:**\n\n#### 1. Make the Vanilla Base:\n1. In a medium saucepan, combine the heavy cream, whole milk, and sugar.\n2. Heat over medium heat, stirring until the sugar dissolves.\n3. Remove from heat and stir in the vanilla extract.\n4. Let the mixture cool slightly, then chill in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour or until cold.\n\n#### 2. Prepare the Chocolate Swirl:\n1. In a small bowl, melt the dark chocolate and set aside to cool slightly.\n2. If using chocolate chips, mix them into the cooled chocolate.\n\n#### 3. Prepare the Strawberry Swirl:\n1. In a saucepan, combine strawberries, sugar, cornstarch, and water.\n2. Cook over medium heat, stirring continuously until the mixture thickens (about 5\u20137 minutes).\n3. Remove from heat and stir in the heavy cream and vanilla extract.\n4. Let the strawberry mixture cool completely.\n\n#### 4. Churn the Ice Cream:\n1. Pour the chilled vanilla base into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions until it reaches a soft-serve consistency (about 20\u201325 minutes).\n2. While the base is churning, prepare the chocolate and strawberry swirls.\n\n#### 5. Add the Swirls:\n1. Once the base is almost ready, stop the churner.\n2. Add the chocolate swirl and fold it in gently.\n3. Return to the churner and continue churning for another 5 minutes.\n4. Then, add the strawberry swirl and mix well.\n\n#### 6. Freeze:\n1. Stop the churner and transfer the mixture to a freezer-safe container.\n2. Cover with a piece of plastic wrap, pressing it directly onto the surface to prevent ice crystals.\n3. Freeze for at least 4 hours or until firm.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf6e **Serving Suggestions:**\n- Serve in a bowl with a spoon.\n- Top with chocolate shavings, fresh strawberries, or a drizzle of chocolate sauce.\n- Store in the freezer for up to 2 weeks.\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you'd like the recipe in **metric units** or with **dairy-free** options!",
